seal     : Before DNA, before proteins, before cells — a single kind of molecule may have done it all. RNA can carry information like a gene and speed reactions like an enzyme, so it can copy itself with no help. The RNA world is the leading guess at life's first chapter: the moment chemistry learned to reproduce, and began.
